-- title:
--   The two-torsion orbit of a triple has full cardinality
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a finite abelian group. Write $H=G[2]=\{u:2u=0\}$, $K=G[3]=\{v:3v=0\}$, $h=|H|$, $t=|K|$, $n=|G|$, and $q=|2G|$. For a triple support $S$, let $\mathcal F(S)$ be all three-element supports having the same ordered pair-sum counts, and $\mathcal O(S)=\{S+u:u\in H\}$. An ordinary fibre has size $h$; an exceptional fibre has size $2h$. For any fibre $F$, put $F^\circ=\{S\in F:0\notin S\}$. For every three-element support $S$,
--
--   $$|\mathcal O(S)|=h.$$
--
--   This describes the finite triple-support square fibres.
-- source:
--   Alexandre Couret, Couret — Additive reconstruction: STROBO-4, singleton collisions and RECOH formal proof artifacts, https://zenodo.org/records/23980513; archive COURET_MATHEMATIQUES_20261105.zip, SHA-256 19a3b59aee930df74cab79c27b29e014843bd17179a26fef1261ed6b5a651ab7; file RECOH/lean/Strobo2TorsCardinality.lean, lines 195–200; source file SHA-256 43bb7bc977683362729a3aa2f7c214abefd9138f3283fb79ee93f0a1da784093; theorem Couret.STROBO2TORS.torsionOrbit_card

